# The flat branch view, through the real window.
#
# What no unit test reaches: that flat is a *mode of the tab* rather than a search. It survives
# navigation, it loses to a live search and comes back when the search is cleared, it comes back
# after a session round trip, and the write verbs a search switches off stay on under it — because
# a flat browse still has a "here" and a search result does not.
#
# The fixture's Documents\Archive\old.txt is three levels down, so no one-level listing can ever
# show it. That is the assertion that cannot pass by accident.

tree .
refresh
assert-not-flat
assert-not-flattened
assert-count 8

# --- Every file at every depth, and no folder rows ---

flat on
assert-flat
assert-flattened
assert-column RelativePath
assert-row old.txt
assert-no-row Documents
assert-count 12
assert-status under
shot 01-flat

# It has a folder being shown, unlike a search result, so New is live and targets the flat root.
# That is exactly the objection that makes New off during a search.
newfile FlatChild.txt
assert-row FlatChild.txt
assert-exists FlatChild.txt

# --- A mode, not a gesture: navigating keeps it ---

go Documents
assert-flat
# still recursive, now from one level down
assert-row old.txt
# and scoped to where we are
assert-no-row notes.txt
back
assert-flat
assert-row notes.txt

# --- A live search wins; clearing it comes back to the flat listing, not the one-level one ---

search old
assert-flattened
assert-row old.txt
clear-search
assert-flat
assert-row notes.txt
assert-row old.txt

# --- The headline case: a whole tree of media as tiles at once ---

thumbnails 0.5
shot 02-flat-thumbnails
thumbnails 0

# --- Survives the session round trip, the way sort and columns do ---

session
assert-flat
assert-row old.txt

# --- The ceiling. A dozen files cannot reach 50,000, so lower it and take the same path. ---
#
# The banner is the point: a status-line suffix is the wrong weight for "you are not seeing all of
# them", which is the one thing a flat view must never leave anyone to assume the other way round.

flat off
flat-cap 4
flat on
assert-count 4
assert-status first
shot 03-flat-truncated

# And the question the real ceiling asks before it ever gets here, worded by the same rule.
dialog flat-large 04-flat-large-folder

flat off
flat-cap 50000

# --- Off puts everything back ---

flat off
assert-not-flat
assert-not-flattened
assert-no-column RelativePath
assert-no-row old.txt
assert-row notes.txt

assert-not-launched
state
